  "A non-match is NOT evidence of absence. Menu prose is marketing, not a recipe: butter, stock, cheese finishes and flour thickeners are routinely unlisted. Every census row carries completeness='text_only_unknown'.",
  "Negation and free-from phrasing ('gluten-free', 'peanut-free', 'no dairy') is detected separately and suppresses the match, but the term list is not exhaustive.",
  "'pea' matches inside 'peach' / 'peanut' only via word-boundary plus longest-match-first ordering; verify on real menus.",
  "'tortilla' is ambiguous: corn (Mexican) vs wheat (flour tortilla) vs egg-and-potato (tortilla espanola). Assigned to multiple categories and flagged ambiguous.",
  "'chips' is ambiguous UK/US (fries vs crisps). Assigned to potato and flagged ambiguous.",
  "Some terms are compound-category by nature (gnocchi is potato AND wheat; injera is teff, a pseudo-grain, listed under wheat_grain for the flour role). Multi-category assignment is intended, not a bug.",
  "No portion size and no quantity is captured. The census counts named ingredients, not amounts.",
  "v0.2 added Spanish/Italian/Amharic terms after validation, but coverage is still uneven and English-first. Addissae's Amharic menu remains the weakest case. Report gaps as a lexicon PR.",
  "Menu spellings are not dictionary spellings. 'Tatertods' was missed by a lexicon that knew 'tater tot'. Expect to add a vendor spelling every time a new corpus lands; a non-match on a dish whose name you recognise is a lexicon bug, not an absent ingredient."
