  {
   "version": "v0.3",
   "utc": "2026-08-23",
   "change": "Validated against the first real menu corpus (299 dishes, 10 Asheville restaurants). Five dishes matched no term; three were genuine gaps and are fixed here. 'Tatertods' -- a menu's own spelling of tater tots -- is why misspellings and vendor spellings matter as much as correct ones. 'Hushpuppies' is a corn starch anchor that was completely invisible, which would have undercounted Southern menus specifically. 'Devils on horseback' is a bacon-wrapped date, so it needed both a cured_meat and a fruit term. The remaining two non-matches are CORRECT: 'Curate Experience' and 'Tasting Menu- $85PP' name no ingredients because they are formats, not dishes -- the format detector handles those, not the lexicon."
